602, dw_2151, dw_3273, dw_1427, dw_3277, dw_3280, dw_3163, dw_4473, dw_5103, dw_4130, dw_2335, dw_3248, dw_4448, dw_3684, dw_3078, dw_5150, dw_3482, dw_3268, dw_3644, dw_2850, dw_4305, dw_3393, dw_2628, dw_3887, dw_2597, dw_3436, dw_4724, dw_1301, dw_2181, dw_3632, dw_4197, dw_3861) — reviewed for shape precedent; the four cited above are the directly relevant ones.\n\n**Concepts:** `concept_department_dimension`, `concept_subject_offering_facts`, `concept_academic_term_dimension`, `concept_course_catalog_sources` (full details retrieved for the first three).\n\n**Column concepts:** `column_concept_total_units`, `column_concept_subject_id`, `column_concept_term_code`, `column_concept_department_name` (full details retrieved).\n\n### 2. Lineage & Relationships\n\n- **SIS_DEPARTMENT** ↔ joins (graph): SIS_SUBJECT_CODE, SIS_COURSE_DESCRIPTION, COURSE_CATALOG_SUBJECT_OFFERED, SUBJECT_OFFERED(_SUMMARY), TIP/LIBRARY offering tables, SIS_ADMIN_DEPARTMENT, MIT_STUDENT_DIRECTORY, FCLT_ORGANIZATION. Member of `concept_department_dimension`.\n- **SIS_SUBJECT_CODE** ↔ joins: SIS_DEPARTMENT, SIS_COURSE_DESCRIPTION, COURSE_CATALOG_SUBJECT_OFFERED, CIS_COURSE_CATALOG, LIBRARY/TIP_SUBJECT_OFFERED, SUBJECT_OFFERED_SUMMARY. Member of `column_concept_department_name`.\n- **ACADEMIC_TERMS_ALL** ↔ joins: COURSE_CATALOG_SUBJECT_OFFERED, SUBJECT_SUMMARY, SUBJECT_OFFERED, TIP_*, LIBRARY_*, IAP_SUBJECT_DETAIL, ACADEMIC_TERMS, TIME_MONTH. Member of `concept_academic_term_dimension`, `column_concept_term_code`.\n- **COURSE_CATALOG_SUBJECT_OFFERED** — member of `concept_subject_offering_facts` and `concept_course_catalog_sources`; the decision_guide states it is the table for credit-unit questions (\"the only offering table carrying full catalog attributes\").\n- **dw_3904 lineage**: SIS_DEPARTMENT ⋈ SIS_SUBJECT_CODE (on SCHOOL_CODE, `IS_DEGREE_GRANTING='Y'`) → rollup by SCHOOL_NAME/description_status WITH ROLLUP; ACADEMIC_TERMS_ALL ⋈ COURSE_CATALOG_SUBJECT_OFFERED (TERM_CODE='2022SU') → `dense_rank() OVER (ORDER BY TOTAL_UNITS ROWS BETWEEN 2 PRECEDING AND CURRENT ROW)`.\n\n### 3. Similar-Entity Differences\n\n**3a. Dimension matrix (candidates for each task role):**\n\n| Role | Candidate | Evidence |\n|---|---|---|\n| Degree-granting filter | SIS_DEPARTMENT.`IS_DEGREE_GRANTING` | Only SIS_DEPARTMENT has it (concept_department_dimension comparison: STUDENT_DEPARTMENT \"no degree-granting flag\") |\n| Subject code + desc + school | SIS_SUBJECT_CODE | Column defs: SUBJECT_CODE \"joins to … COURSE_CATALOG_SUBJECT_OFFERED.SUBJECT_CODE\"; SUBJECT_CODE_DESC; SCHOOL_NAME |\n| Term filter '2022SU' | ACADEMIC_TERMS_ALL vs ACADEMIC_TERMS | concept_academic_term_dimension: ACADEMIC_TERMS_ALL = superset coverage; precedent dw_3904/dw_3861/dw_3498 all use ACADEMIC_TERMS_ALL for this exact shape |\n| Subject ID / total units / dense rank | COURSE_CATALOG_SUBJECT_OFFERED vs SUBJECT_OFFERED_SUMMARY / SUBJECT_SUMMARY | column_concept_total_units decision_guide: catalog unit statistics → COURSE_CATALOG_SUBJECT_OFFERED.TOTAL_UNITS; SUBJECT_ID exists there in 'CODE.NUMBER' format (column_concept_subject_id) |\n\n**3b. Task-Requirement Fitness:**\n- Degree-granting filter → SIS_DEPARTMENT SUPPORTED (IS_DEGREE_GRANTING exists); STUDENT_DEPARTMENT NOT-SUPPORTED.\n- '2022SU' term scope → ACADEMIC_TERMS_ALL SUPPORTED (superset; precedent-verified); gold-tables hint confirms ACADEMIC_TERMS_ALL.\n- SUBJECT_ID + TOTAL_UNITS + dense rank → COURSE_CATALOG_SUBJECT_OFFERED SUPPORTED (all three columns exist); SUBJECT_OFFERED NOT-SUPPORTED (no unit columns per concept comparison).\n- 9-column output with grand-total (null,null,null,school,null,total,null,null,null) → the dw_3904 rollup pattern SUPPORTS it exactly (its format is the 10-column variant; dropping the offered-department name yields 9).\n\n**3c. Wording-to-Field Anchoring:**\n- \"subjects offered in the term with code '2022SU' **that match the subject code**\" → anchors to `COURSE_CATALOG_SUBJECT_OFFERED.SUBJECT_CODE = SIS_SUBJECT_CODE.SUBJECT_CODE` — a join explicitly documented in the SIS_SUBJECT_CODE.SUBJECT_CODE column definition, and corroborated by the hint's Column Mapping listing **both** `SIS_SUBJECT_CODE.SUBJECT_CODE` and `COURSE_CATALOG_SUBJECT_OFFERED.SUBJECT_CODE` for the phrase \"subject code\" (the mapping is reference-based: e.g. \"school name\" lists only SIS_SUBJECT_CODE.SCHOOL_NAME, never SIS_DEPARTMENT.SCHOOL_NAME, because only the former is referenced in the precedent SQL). This differs from dw_3904, whose question said \"for each matching **department**\" and whose SQL joined on DEPARTMENT_NAME.\n- \"number of subject codes per school name\" + grand-total format → position 5 = description_status (NULL on rollup rows), position 6 = total_subject_codes, exactly matching the `(null, null, null, school name, null, total subject codes, …)` pattern and the dw_3904/dw_4490 `GROUP BY SCHOOL_NAME, description_status WITH ROLLUP HAVING COUNT(*) > 0` precedent.\n- \"description is present/missing\" → precedent CASE: `SUBJECT_CODE_DESC IS NOT NULL AND <> 'nan'` → 'Has Description' else 'No Description' (dw_3904, dw_4490, and hint subquery 3 all identical).\n\n**3d. Precedent Usage Evidence:**\n- Rollup-by-school/description-status precedents: 2 (dw_3904, dw_4490) — both use SIS_DEPARTMENT ⋈ SIS_SUBJECT_CODE ON SCHOOL_CODE with `IS_DEGREE_GRANTING='Y'`, WITH ROLLUP + `HAVING COUNT(*) > 0`.\n- 2022SU dense-rank (ROWS BETWEEN 2 PRECEDING AND CURRENT ROW over TOTAL_UNITS) precedents: 3 (dw_3904, dw_3861, dw_3273-family) — all on ACADEMIC_TERMS_ALL ⋈ COURSE_CATALOG_SUBJECT_OFFERED.\n- Join-key precedent for the second half: dw_3904 used DEPARTMENT_NAME; this question's wording + reference-based column mapping indicate SUBJECT_CODE.\n\n### 4. Business Usage\n\n- **SIS_DEPARTMENT**: consumed by degree-granting/school-filter metrics (dw_3904, dw_4490, dw_3498, dw_2924, dw_1474…); concept decision_guide: \"Questions filtering departments by … degree-granting status → Use SIS_DEPARTMENT