N it on **SUBJECT_CODE** (per the question's \"that match the subject code\" and the reference-based column mapping). Output exactly 9 columns in the grand-total order.\n\n**6c. Reasons:** *Data* — SIS_SUBJECT_CODE.SUBJECT_CODE's definition documents the join to COURSE_CATALOG_SUBJECT_OFFERED.SUBJECT_CODE; TOTAL_UNITS/SUBJECT_ID exist only in the catalog table among 2022SU-scope candidates. *Semantic-network* — concept decision guides select SIS_DEPARTMENT (degree-granting), ACADEMIC_TERMS_ALL (widest term coverage), COURSE_CATALOG_SUBJECT_OFFERED (unit statistics); dw_3904 supplies the verbatim rollup/window SQL. *Business* — the 'Has Description'/'No Description' + WITH ROLLUP grand-total pattern is an established question family (dw_3904, dw_4490).\n\n**6d. Tie-breaker note:** dw_3904 joined the second half on DEPARTMENT_NAME, but its question said \"matching department\"; this question says \"match the subject code\" and the hint's column mapping references COURSE_CATALOG_SUBJECT_OFFERED.SUBJECT_CODE — so the SUBJECT_CODE join is used. If live data were reachable, join-match rates would confirm; the DB is inaccessible (auth failure), so the wording + mapping evidence decides.\n\n",
